SUMMARY:Beyond Gray Walls: An IU Prison Arts Student Exhibit
DESCRIPTION:IUPAI proudly presents our newest exhibition "Behind Gray Wal
 ls\," showcasing students' artwork and writing produced over the last yea
 r. Our opening reception is on December 4th from 5-8 pm during Gallery Wa
 lk.  Larissa Danielle taught two visual art courses\, both in the summers
  of 2025 and 2026 respectively. We will feature 6 physical paintings from
  her latest class!  Kenny Mitchell taught a creative writing course in Sp
 ring 2026. Three original works written by his students will be presented
  through a listening booth separate from the art exhibit.  Monetary donat
 ions will be accepted at the opening reception. A talk will be given by I
 UPAI's Program Coordinator\, David Bandera. Food and drink will be provid
 ed! Be sure to attend and offer your support!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  IUPAI proudly presents our newest exhib
 ition "Behind Gray Walls\," showcasing students' artwork and writing prod
 uced over the last year. Our opening reception is on December 4th from 5-
 8 pm during Gallery Walk.</p><p>  Larissa Danielle taught two visual art 
 courses\, both in the summers of 2025 and 2026 respectively. We will feat
 ure 6 physical paintings from her latest class!</p><p>  Kenny Mitchell ta
 ught a creative writing course in Spring 2026. Three original works writt
 en by his students will be presented through a listening booth separate f
 rom the art exhibit.</p><p>  Monetary donations will be accepted at the o
 pening reception. A talk will be given by IUPAI's Program Coordinator\, D
 avid Bandera. Food and drink will be provided! Be sure to attend and offe
 r your support!</p>
