SUMMARY:Grant Writing 101 and Public Funding for the Arts
DESCRIPTION:Have a big artistic vision\, passion project\, or community a
 rts idea—and zero clue how to pay for it? Or maybe you need introductor
 y skills in understanding the application process for your future career?
   Forget dry lectures and confusing jargon. This interactive session brea
 ks down the real-world basics of getting your creative work funded. We'll
  cover:Decoding Public Funding: How city\, state\, and federal arts funde
 rs work—and how to find opportunities built for emerging artists and or
 ganizers.  Making Data Your Superpower: How to gather and use compelling 
 data to back up your creative vision and make your grant applications sta
 nd out from the pile.  Zero experience is required!Whether you've never l
 ooked at a grant application in your life or just want to level up your r
 esume\, this workshop builds the foundational skills you need to start ap
 plying with confidence.  This workshop kicks off a three-part series desi
 gned to take you through the entire funding journey\, continuing in Sprin
 g 2027. You can attend just one workshop or join us for all three!Worksho
 p 1 (December 11):Grant Writing 101 &amp\; Public Funding for the Arts �
 � Public funding essentials (city\, state\, federal) and using data to st
 rengthen your application.  Workshop 2 (Spring 2027):Foundation Funding f
 or the Arts — Exploring local and regional foundation opportunities\, b
 uilding genuine funder relationships\, and crafting a standout story.  Wo
 rkshop 3 (Spring 2027):Communicating Impact in the Arts and Culture Secto
 r — Mastering the grant cycle before and after you win the award\, incl
 uding practical skills in evaluation planning\, documentation\, and impac
 t reporting.
