SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Zines and Themes (AM Session)
DESCRIPTION:By looking at artworks in the galleries and how they are crea
 ted\, selected\, and displayed\, students will discover how meaning can b
 e built through organization and connection. Students will then get to cr
 eate their own thematic zine – a small handmade booklet that brings ima
 ges and ideas together. Join us to experiment\, curate\, and design a zin
 e inspired by your own unique theme!  Program designed by our licensed ar
 t educator for students in grades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in th
 e Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum. Together\,
  we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries. After seei
 ng artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm 
 Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to 
 dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask that
  chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  By looking at artworks in the galleries
  and how they are created\, selected\, and displayed\, students will disc
 over how meaning can be built through organization and connection. Studen
 ts will then get to create their own thematic zine – a small handmade b
 ooklet that brings images and ideas together. Join us to experiment\, cur
 ate\, and design a zine inspired by your own unique theme!</p><p>  Progra
 m designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.</p><
 p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Cen
 ter for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum. Together\, we'll drop o
 ff personal items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks t
 hat will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Ma
 king Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a m
 ess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> 
 We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 childr
 en.</p>
